# Users — main endpoints. Generated skeleton, synthetic data only.
# Path ids below are placeholders — replace with real ids from a list call.
@user = 1
# Variables: see rest/http-client.env.json (host, session, xsrf). How to get them: docs/guides/api.md
# Full list of Users operations: /api/docs (tag "Users").

### GET /api/users — users.index
GET {{host}}/api/users
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{session_cookie_name}}={{session}}; XSRF-TOKEN={{xsrf}}

### POST /api/users — users.store
POST {{host}}/api/users
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{session_cookie_name}}={{session}}; XSRF-TOKEN={{xsrf}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrf}}
Referer: {{host}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
    "name": "Example name",
    "role": "admin"
}

### PATCH /api/users/{user} — users.update
PATCH {{host}}/api/users/{{user}}
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{session_cookie_name}}={{session}}; XSRF-TOKEN={{xsrf}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrf}}
Referer: {{host}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "role": "admin",
    "status": "active",
    "branch_ids": [
        1
    ],
    "safe_speak_handler": true
}

### PATCH /api/users/{user} — make another user a superadmin (HRM-84; superadmin only, never oneself)
# Expected: 200, data.roles contains "superadmin"; audit "role_changed". Admin/hr_manager/others → 403.
PATCH {{host}}/api/users/{{user}}
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{session_cookie_name}}={{session}}; XSRF-TOKEN={{xsrf}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrf}}
Referer: {{host}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "roles": ["superadmin", "admin"]
}

### PATCH /api/users/{user} — take superadmin back (the last active superadmin → 422 last_superadmin)
PATCH {{host}}/api/users/{{user}}
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{session_cookie_name}}={{session}}; XSRF-TOKEN={{xsrf}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrf}}
Referer: {{host}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "roles": ["admin"]
}

### POST /api/users — invite a superadmin (HRM-84)
POST {{host}}/api/users
Accept: application/json
Cookie: {{session_cookie_name}}={{session}}; XSRF-TOKEN={{xsrf}}
X-XSRF-TOKEN: {{xsrf}}
Referer: {{host}}/
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "second.owner@example.com",
    "name": "Second Owner",
    "role": "superadmin"
}
